. 
. * Note: bacondecomp requires a balanced panel and an absorbing (weakly monoto
> nic) treatment. IMP_UNILATERAL is already absorbing by construction.
. * We use init_stpop as weights for consistency with the regression above.
. 
. * Goodman-Bacon decomposes the TWFE estimator into a weighted average of DiD 
> comparisons (treated vs not-treated, early treatment vs late treatment and la
> te treatment vs early treatment). Some components may receive problematic wei
> ghts (negative or because already-treated units are used as controls), which 
> we will now check for our estimator.
. 
. * The Never-treated vs. timing comparison dominates the TFWE coefficient (wei
> ght of 0.88)
. * All individual weights in the decomposition are positive, so there is no ev
> idence of negative weights.
. * However, there is significant heterogeneity (from -1.1 to +1.5) in the 2×2 
> DiD estimates of timing-group comparisons (Early vs. Late and Late vs. Early)
> , with some negative estimates receiving small but non-zero weights. This het
> erogeneity suggests that treatment effects vary across cohorts and over time.
>  
. 
. *POINT I
. 
. *step 1: create unilateral divorce dummies
