. 
. *Interpretation: Across all three specifications, pre-treatment coefficients 
> are close to zero and insignificant, supporting the parallel trends assumptio
> n. Post-treatment, we observe a temporary spike in divorce rates in the first
>  8 years following the reform, which then fades and becomes insignificant — s
> omething the single-coefficient analysis in point (e) could not detect, as it
>  was averaging over this entire dynamic response into one number.
. 
. *POINT J
. 
. *ssc install coefplot
. set scheme s1color

. 
. * Plot all 3 specifications on the same graph using stored estimates.
. coefplot (es_1, label("No trends")) ///
>          (es_2, label("Linear trends")) ///
>          (es_3, label("Quadratic trends")), ///
>          keep(D_lag* D_lead*) vertical yline(0) ///
>          xtitle("Years relative to treatment") ///
>          ytitle("Effect on divorce rate (per 1,000 persons)") ///
>          title("Event Study: Unilateral Divorce Laws") ///
