. 
. 
. * Corrections performed by proposed algorithm:
. * Sun & Abraham (2021) corrects the contamination problem in standard TWFE ev
> ent-study regressions. The IW estimator instead:
. * (i)  estimates cohort-specific effects by interacting each relative-time du
> mmy with cohort indicators (i.e. the year of treatment adoption)
. * (ii) aggregates these cohort-specific effects using sample-share weights, e
> nsuring all weights are non-negative.
. 
. * Results consistency: 
. * Results based on the Sun & Abraham (2021) correction are consistent with Wo
> lfers (2006): pre-treatment coefficients are close to zero (supporting parall
> el trends), divorce rates spike temporarily in the first years following refo
> rm before returning to baseline. We later observe negative coefficients beyon
> d year 8, also consistent with Wolfers' findings of a potential reversal. How
> ever, he cautions against drawing conclusions about long-run effects (as unde
> rlined in POINT K).
. * In particular, note that consistency holds mainly for the only FE and FE+ti
> me trends, while there is an increase in uncertainty when adding the quadrati
> c time trend which makes the coefficient estimate more noisy (especially for 
> the dummy D^+15). 
. 
. 
. 
